ph.md": "e1dc10ac0d6bbba23b47c431cc66fdf3eb99521bfb9e95e9e32c5567aa57bb5c", "notes/tt-mass-adjoint-certificate.md": "03967fae55d1d4a36c358c3cae499a42762c1592a12db93bafc589fb68876c33", "notes/tt-mass-numerical-bound.md": "9026b1269a63339e00bc69a2b1ea30ff7dc50878f2de1cc9b83e3c4ee33de844", "notes/uniform-dirac-reference.md": "a8214316cb9a7338680b55b92c446fa201c93f82f31dd0c7e94a2847296a361b", "notes/uniform-logarithmic-frequency-comparison.md": "c2e2cb216d45a508dcabe8ac0709f790f4631174ce32d40bfc4cbc62f5fbefc8", "notes/ward-sources-and-fast-compatibility.md": "fe77cf54525be57b0156c4c9d6e3f11e4ab41bfa1682b2a5b0f3b1bcaa54e8ba", "notes/weighted-normal-inverse-scale.md": "70c569775adce691d2d7e9b7a91a92591d43983bce64f1d287b22aeb4c48ea46", "notes/weighted-york-source-conversion.md": "4ed978cfaf69b04a01356d83619b9445b568eb945540a83e12b343e6d1212175"}, "frozen_sources_utf8": {"notes/current-magnetic-reference-reconstruction.md": "# Reconstruct a prescribed source component before choosing the next solve\n\n2026-10-24, E003/S169. Ordinary argument before acceptance execution.\nThe full stable semiclassical wormhole objective remains active and incomplete;\nthe feasibility audit stays closed. This is a component of the actual reference\ncorrection, not the full quantum correction or a freely chosen forcing.\n\n## 1. What this calculation can decide\n\nThe previous localized adjoint test requires |I_g|<1.06655e-54 for the\ncurrent uniform .0022 certificate, even with the entire bolt error budget.\nThe complete available allowance, 1.3079691e-40, is not a measured value.\nBefore interpreting that gap, reconstruct the response to the exactly\nspecified product-matched magnetic potential J_M. Its coefficient is\nk=G q^2/(12 pi C B^2), not an adjustable coupling. Use precisely the\ndecomposition J=J_M+J_rest of current-product-matched-source-projection.md.\n\nLet h_M solve I0'' h_M=-J_M'(g0), with the same fixed clock, temperature,\nfinite geometry and reference boundary action. The actual full first\ncorrection decomposes h1=h_M+h_rest. This linear identity does NOT identify\nh_M with h1. In particular the full-action residual of h_M/F_lambda is\n\n    f_rest + J'' h_M/F_lambda,\n\nwhere f_rest=J_rest'(g0). The first-order term f_rest must not be omitted.\nThe selected full residual projection is\n\n    I_g = P_MM + P_cross,\n    P_MM = J_M''[h_M,(v,-z^4)]/(F_lambda W),\n    P_cross = {J_M''h_rest + J_rest''h_M + J_rest''h_rest}\n                                      [(v,-z^4)]/(F_lambda W).\n\nHere v is the SAME global scalar-return test. No rest source is being\nselected to cancel a residual. We execute P_MM, including the existing\nscalar-trial error, and give a numerical target for the still unknown\nP_cross. Passing this necessary projection screen is not a bolt certificate.\n\n## 2. Exact reconstruction on the actual finite-temperature geometry\n\nPut t=r/B, v_h=1+h, z=1/t, z_h=1/v_h, F(t)=C t^2 Q(1/t), and\n\n    g(t)=4/t-3/t^2-1-2 log(t),\n    A(z)=(3-2 log z)z-2z^2+z^3-2,  A'(z)=-g(1/z).\n\nJ_M is a covariant radius potential. Its complete orbit source satisfies\n\n    rho_M=-k C g(t)/(2G t^2),  p_M=-rho_M,  a_M=0.\n\nThe angular source is the derivative of this same potential, so the\nreference Ward identity is retained. Write sigma=delta R/B. The exact\nfixed-temperature constraint solution is\n\n    sigma=-k C g(v_h)/[v_h^2(v_h F_tt(v_h)+F_t(v_h))],\n    f_M(t)={-2 C gamma v_h sigma\n                   +k C[A(1/t)-A(z_h)]}/t,\n    w_M(t)=-F(t) integral_t^infinity f_M(s)/F(s)^2 ds,\n    nu_M=w_M/t,  b_M=w_M,t/2-w_M/t.                 (1)\n\nBoth horizon equations hold: f_M(v_h)+2C gamma sigma=0 and\nf_M,t(v_h)+F_tt(v_h)sigma=0. Set fbar=f_M+sigma F_t and H=fbar/F.\nThen t fbar and its first derivative vanish at v_h. Thus H(v_h)=0;\nthe equivalent formula w_M=sigma-F integral_t^infinity H/F has no\nlogarithmic bolt singularity. It follows that w_M(v_h)=sigma and the\nfields are regular radial disk fields. No inner wall is introduced.\n\nAt infinity f_M=const/t+O(log(t)/t^2). Consequently nu_M and b_M have\ntheir allowed cubic mass terms followed by z^4 log z terms, with all\nfive weighted derivatives. They have zero leading clock/scalar source.\nThis checks the domain of this PARTICULAR tangent; it proves neither\nadmission of the nonlinear X ball nor a strong inverse for the full source.\nThe original paired quantum realization is unchanged and is not replaced\nby a smooth double or a selection of modes.\n\n## 3. Complete, conservative bounds for this reconstructed tangent\n\nThe identities g(1)=g_t(1)=0 and\ng_t=-2(t-1)(t+3)/t^3 give |g|<=4(t-1)^2 and\n|(g/t^2)_t|<=16. The actual parameter intervals in (1) give\n0<sigma/k<3h^2. For N=t fbar,\n\n    |N_tt| <= k C(16+30h^2),  N(v_h)=N_t(v_h)=0.\n\nUse the retained whole-geometry inequalities\nF>=.99x(t-v_h)(t-1), |2F_tt+tF_ttt|<10C, x=lambda B^2.\nThey imply\n\n    |H| <= [(8+15h^2)C/(.99x)] k <49k,\n    |w_M| <=3kh^2+98k(t-1),  |nu_M|<99k.         (2)\n\nThe second estimate uses the already proved\nF(t) integral_t^infinity ds/F(s)<=2(t-1). For t-v_h>=h the independent\ngeometric bounds F_t integral 1/F<16 and (F/t) integral 1/F<10 give\n|b_M|<(1/2+10)49k+3kh^2<515k.\nFor 0<=y=t-v_h<=h, (1) instead gives |H|<4.1k y/h. The exact convex\nlower bound F>=2C gamma y+.95x y^2 gives\n\n    |integral_t^infinity H/F| <= (4.1+2.8*49)k/(2C gamma).\n\nHere log(1+2C gamma/(.95xh))<2.8. Also\nF_t<=2C gamma+12.1xh and F<=2C gamma h+6.05xh^2.\nSubstitution in b_M=H/2-sigma/t-(F_t/2-F/t)integral H/F gives\n|b_M|<170k there. Use the global bound |b_M|<600k.\nAll constants are numerical substitutions into actual geometry bounds,\nnot a new source normalization. The physical bolt functional is\n\n    |L_b h_M|=sigma/h<3kh.                         (3)\n\n## 4. Certified signed integration, with the endpoints retained\n\nUse the previously frozen fractional scalar trial v_p, with its original\ncoefficients. Let g now denote g(1/z), g_phi=-2(1-z)(1+3z), and\n\n    K_w=z^2 g_phi v_p'-8g z^5,\n    k_b=2g_phi v_p-4g z^4.\n\nSince a_M=0, integration by parts on [0,z_c], z_c=1-2^-49, gives\n\n    P_MM,bulk = k/F_lambda [integral_0^zc w_M K_w dz\n                                  -zc^2 k_b(zc)w_M(zc)/2].   (4)\n\nThe outer endpoint vanishes in the actual mass/log phase. The finite\nz_c endpoint is INCLUDED. On [z_c,z_h] use the ORIGINAL mixed density\nk[(g_phiphi v_p-2g_phi z^4)nu_M+(2g_phi v_p-4g z^4)b_M], not a\ndiscontinuous test or a new boundary condition.\n\nThe exact nested integral in z is\n\n    w_M/k = Q(z)/z^2 integral_0^z s^3[-A(s)+A(z_h)\n                                  +2 gamma v_h sigma/k]/Q(s)^2 ds. (5)\n\nIts integrand is nonnegative. Evaluate Q with its factored polynomial\nand the ORIGINAL nonzero thermal term; retain correlated gamma,h,z_h.\nMonotone endpoint values bound A and g on each cell. Cumulative lower\nand upper rectangle integrals bound (5), including every intermediate\npoint of a cell. Signed interval products then enclose (4). The scalar\ntrial and (1-z)v_p' use the earlier degree-six Taylor/Bernstein enclosure,\nwith its explicit seventh-derivative remainder. This is a whole-interval\nquadrature proof, not point sampling.\n\nOn 0<z<z_o=2^-20, Q>beta/2 and -A(z)+A(z_h)+2gamma v_h sigma/k<3;\nthus the initial integral lies in [0,3z_o^4/beta^2]. The existing\nabsolute scalar-trial coefficient sum gives the analytic contribution\nbound with integral z^4 |log z|. For the last cold interval, (2) gives\n|nu_M|/k<=3h^2+98(1-z_c)/z_c; use |g_phi|<=8(1-z_c),\n|g|<=4(1-z_c)^2/z_c, |g_phiphi|<=8 and |v_p|<1.01.\nThese are full endpoint allowances, not omitted cold physics.\n\nFinally transfer from v_p to the actual v. The retained scalar inverse\ncertificate bounds ||v-v_p||L2(z^-4 dz)<3.6891662e-12. The scalar row of\nJ_M''h_M is k(g_phiphi nu_M+2g_phi b_M). Since |g_phi|<=3,\n|g_phiphi|<=8, (2) and |b_M|<600k give its dual weighted norm\n<=4392 k^2/sqrt(5). Therefore add\n\n    E_scalar,M <= (4392/sqrt(5)) k^2(3.6891662e-12)/F_lambda.  (6)\n\nThis uses the existing scalar solve; no scalar optimization is selected.\n\n## 5. Decision rule and claims boundary\n\nThe first frozen run rejected the bolt shift: independently evaluating\ng(z_h) lost its exact double zero and produced an interval wider than\nh^2. Preserve that failure. Evaluate the SAME function for z>1/2 as\ng=-4y^2-sum_(j=3)^48 2y^j/j, y=1-z, with tail at most\n2y^49/[49(1-y)]. Likewise A=-4y^3/3-sum_(j=3)^48\n2y^(j+1)/[j(j+1)], with tail at most 2y^50/[49*50*(1-y)].\nBoth are convergent identities with their entire tails retained. This\npreserves the shared bolt parameter; it changes no source or temperature.\n\nFreeze acceptance at a complete |P_MM|<3e-57. Independently, (2) and the\nprevious certified I_w bound give a conservative check <3e-57 without\nthe signed quadrature. Compare both with the actual localized ceiling.\nIf the component is far below that ceiling, the oversized original\nallowance is not evidence that THIS source component forces failure.\nIt still supplies no bound for P_cross or the complete correction.\n\nThe decisive outstanding calculation becomes the reconstruction of\nh_rest=-I0''^-1 J_rest'(g0) on the actual paired domain, retaining its\nmass/log endpoint expansion and full thermal/angular/contact source.\nThis is the missing input to the coupled directional forward/adjoint\nsolve, not permission to replace that solve by h_M. First-order source\nevaluation and its strong weighted return take priority over optimizing\nthe already passing cold/scalar/quantum projection bounds.\n\nThe known excessive upper allowance, unknown actual P_cross, and proved\nfailure of a uniform V* to C5 admission bound are three different facts.\nNone proves physical nonexistence. The qualitative C2 action on bounded\nADMITTED stationary families remains valid in its existing scope.\nY0+1e-8 Z0+5e-17 Z2<=1e-8 and Z0+1e-8 Z2<1 remain unclosed;\nY0<=5e-9, Z0<=.25, Z2<=5e7 remain sufficient unproved allocations.\nThe actual <1.667e-9 bolt difference, strong admission margins, exact\ncompatibility, physical matching/causal realization, semiclassical\nvalidity/noise and all-sector stability are not established here.\n\nRemaining to-do list: reconstruct the complete remaining prescribed source\nand correction with weighted error; coupled directional forward/adjoint\ncertificate and nonlinear admission; exact compatibility; physical matching\nand causal realization; semiclassical validity/noise and all-sector stability;\ncharge/return, opening, transport, preparation, separate creation and the\nfull stable-wormhole objective.\n", "checks/current_magnetic_reference_reconstruction.py": "\"\"\"Actual finite-geometry prescribed magnetic reference response, not h1.\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom hashlib import sha256\nfrom datetime import datetime,timezone\nimport sys,json,traceback\nif '--arb-path' in sys.argv:sys.path.insert(0,sys.argv[sys.argv.index('--arb-path')+1])\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];sys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'checks'))\nimport current_product_matched_source_projection as old\nimport sympy as sp\nfrom flint import arb,ctx\nSTEM='current-magnetic-reference-reconstruction'\nOWN=['notes/'+STEM+'.md','checks/current_magnetic_reference_reconstruction.py','evidence/'+STEM+'-review.json']\nROWS=[];enc=old.encoded;dec=old.decode\ndef check(name,ok,detail=''):\n ROWS.append(dict(name=name,passed=bool(ok),detail=str(detail)))\n if not ok:raise AssertionError(name)\ndef digest(p):return sha256((ROOT/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\ndef hull(lo,hi):return arb((lo+hi)/2,(hi-lo)/2)\ndef g(z):\n if not z>arb('.5'):return old.g(z)\n y=1-z;value=-4*y*y;yp=y*y\n for j in range(3,49):\n  yp*=y;value-=2*yp/j\n return value+arb(0,(2*yp*y/(49*(1-y))).abs_upper())\ndef A(z):\n if not z>arb('.5'):return (3-2*z.log())*z-2*z*z+z**3-2\n y=1-z;value=-arb(4)/3*y**3;yp=y**3\n for j in range(3,49):\n  yp*=y;value-=2*yp/(j*(j+1))\n return value+arb(0,(2*yp*y/(49*50*(1-y))).abs_upper())\ndef Q(p,z):return (1-z)**2*(p['beta']*(1+2*z+3*z*z)+p['u']*z*z+p['eps']*z**4)-p['tau']*z**3\ndef algebra():\n t,z,k,C,ga,vh,ss=sp.symbols('t z k C gamma v sigma',positive=True)\n gg=4/t-3/t**2-1-2*sp.log(t);aa=(3-2*sp.log(z))*z-2*z*z+z**3-2\n check('primitive_identity',sp.simplify(sp.diff(aa,z)+gg.subs(t,1/z))==0)\n check('source_double_product_zero',gg.subs(t,1)==0 and sp.diff(gg,t).subs(t,1)==0)\n check('signed_source_derivative',sp.simplify(sp.diff(gg,t)+2*(t-1)*(t+3)/t**3)==0)\n f=(-2*C*ga*vh*ss+k*C*(aa.subs(z,1/t)-aa.subs(z,1/vh)))/t\n check('first_reference_constraint',sp.simplify(sp.diff(t*f,t)-k*C*gg/t**2)==0)\n check('moving_bolt_constraint',sp.simplify(f.subs(t,vh)+2*C*ga*ss)==0)\n ftt=sp.symbols('Ftt')\n sig=-k*C*gg.subs(t,vh)/(vh**2*(vh*ftt+2*C*ga))\n check('fixed_temperature_constraint',sp.simplify((sp.diff(f,t).subs(t,vh)+ftt*ss).subs(ss,sig))==0)\n ww,ff=sp.Function('w')(t),sp.Function('F')(t)\n # Differentiating -F times the outward Green integral gives this ODE.\n check('fixed_chart_displacement_ODE',sp.simplify(sp.diff(-ff*sp.Integral(f/ff**2,(t,t,sp.oo)),t)-(-sp.diff(ff,t)*sp.Integral(f/ff**2,(t,t,sp.oo))+f/ff))==0)\n\ndef execute():\n algebra();p,h,zh,env=old.scalar.prev.york.actual_parameters()\n C,B2,x,ga=p['C'],p['B2'],p['g']*p['B2'],p['gamma'];vh=1+h\n k=arb(p['q'])**2/(12*arb.pi()*C*B2);Fl=p['Fl'];zo=arb(2)**-20;yc=arb(2)**-49;zc=1-yc\n z=sp.symbols('z');qexpr=(1-z)**2*(sp.Symbol('b')*(1+2*z+3*z*z)+sp.Symbol('u')*z*z+sp.Symbol('e')*z**4)-sp.Symbol('ta')*z**3\n # Exact coefficient evaluation; use Q(zh)=0 and Q'(zh)=-2 gamma.\n q2=2*p['u']+6*(-4*p['beta']-2*p['u']-p['tau'])*zh+12*(3*p['beta']+p['u']+p['eps'])*zh**2-40*p['eps']*zh**3+30*p['eps']*zh**4\n sigbar=-g(zh)*zh**2/(6*ga+zh*q2)\n check('actual_positive_bolt_shift',sigbar>0 and sigbar<3*h*h)\n Hbar=(8+15*h*h)*C/(arb('.99')*x)\n check('global_reference_shape_bound',Hbar<49)\n check('inner_regular_H_bound',(4+arb('7.5')*h*h)*h/ga<arb('4.1'))\n tail_log=(1+2*C*ga/(arb('.95')*x*h)).log()\n check('inner_outward_Green_tail',tail_log<arb('2.8'))\n Jbar=(arb('4.1')+arb('2.8')*49)/(2*C*ga)\n b_inner=arb(49)/2+3*h*h+((2*C*ga+arb('12.1')*x*h)/2+(2*C*ga*h+arb('6.05')*x*h*h))*Jbar\n check('inner_shape_amplitude',b_inner<170)\n check('outer_shape_amplitude',(arb('.5')+10)*49+3*h*h<515)\n check('outer_Q_guard',Q(p,hull(arb(0),zo))>p['beta']/2)\n seeddata=json.loads((ROOT/'evidence/current-schur-scalar-projection.json').read_bytes())['runs'][-1]\n row=next(r for r in seeddata['numerics'] if r['kind']=='actual_global_scalar_inverse')\n old.scalar.power=dec(row['fractional_power']);old.scalar.y0=h/(1+h)\n trial=old.scalar.FP({(r['z_power'],r['y_integer_power'],r['fractional_multiplicity']):dec(r['coefficient']) for r in row['trial_coefficients']})+old.scalar.mon(4)/2\n power=old.scalar.power;n=max(i for i,j,t in trial.c)\n P=[trial.c.get((i,0,0),arb(0)) for i in range(n+1)];T=[trial.c.get((i,0,1),arb(0)) for i in range(n+1)]\n AP=[arb(0) for _ in P];BT=[arb(0) for _ in P]\n for i in range(n+1):\n  if i:AP[i-1]+=i*P[i];BT[i-1]+=i*T[i]\n  AP[i]-=i*P[i];BT[i]-=(i+power)*T[i]\n C1=sum((a.abs_upper() for a in AP+BT),arb(0))\n initial=[(arb(2)**-j,arb(2)**(-j+1)) for j in range(20,1,-1)]\n initial +=[(1-arb(2)**(-j+1),1-arb(2)**-j) for j in range(2,50)]\n shift=A(zh)+2*ga*vh*sigbar\n check('outer_numerator_guard',2+shift.abs_upper()<3)\n Slo=arb(0);Shi=3*zo**4/p['beta']**2;integ=arb(0);cells=[];sub=128\n for band,(left,right) in enumerate(initial):\n  for j in range(sub):\n   lo=left+(right-left)*j/sub;hi=left+(right-left)*(j+1)/sub;zz=hull(lo,hi);width=hi-lo\n   qq=Q(p,zz);check_positive=qq.lower()>0\n   if not check_positive:raise AssertionError('positive_full_Q_'+str(band)+'_'+str(j))\n   aa=hull(A(lo).lower(),A(hi).upper());num=-aa+shift\n   if not num.lower()>0:raise AssertionError('positive_full_integrand_'+str(band)+'_'+str(j))\n   ii=zz**3*num/qq**2\n   Srange=hull(Slo.lower(),(Shi+width*ii.upper()).upper())\n   wbar=qq/zz**2*Srange\n   bern=[old.bern_on_cell(c,lo,hi) for c in [P,T,AP,BT]]\n   vv=old.family_bound(bern[0],bern[1],lo,hi,power)\n   yvp=old.family_bound(bern[2],bern[3],lo,hi,power)\n   gg=hull(g(lo).lower(),g(hi).upper())\n   kw=-2*zz**2*(1+3*zz)*yvp-8*gg*zz**5\n   val=wbar*kw*width;integ+=val\n   Slo+=width*ii.lower();Shi+=width*ii.upper()\n   cells.append(dict(lo=enc(lo),hi=enc(hi),inner_integrand=enc(ii),w_over_k=enc(wbar),signed_integral=enc(val)))\n  if band%12==0:print(json.dumps(dict(event='actual_nested_integral_band',band=band,cells=len(cells),integral=str(integ))),flush=True)\n check('whole_bulk_coverage',len(cells)==len(initial)*sub and initial[0][0]==zo and initial[-1][1]==zc)\n wend=Q(p,zc)/zc**2*hull(Slo.lower(),Shi.upper())\n gp=-2*yc*(1+3*zc);kb=2*gp*trial.value(zc)-4*g(zc)*zc**4\n endpoint=-zc**2*kb*wend/2\n logm=zo**5*(arb(1)/25-zo.log()/5)\n outer=98*((8*C1+64)*zo**5/5+16*logm)+3*h*h*((8*C1+64)*zo**6/6+16*zo**6*(arb(1)/36-zo.log()/6))\n n_cold=3*h*h+98*yc/zc\n kn=arb('8.08')+16*yc;kbmax=arb('16.16')*yc+16*yc*yc/zc\n cold=yc*(kn*n_cold+kbmax*600)\n scalarE=4392/arb(5).sqrt()*arb('3.6891662e-12')\n value=k*k/Fl*(integ+endpoint);error=k*k/Fl*(outer+cold+scalarE)\n enclosure=value+arb(0,error.upper())\n olddata=json.loads((ROOT/'evidence/current-product-matched-source-projection.json').read_bytes())['runs'][-1]\n r=next(a for a in olddata['numerics'] if a['kind']=='validated_magnetic_weak_integrals')\n iw=dec(r['integral_enclosures'][1]);raw=dec(r['raw_absolute_kernel_integral_bounds'][1])\n direct=k*k/Fl*(98*iw.upper()+3*h*h*raw+endpoint.abs_upper()+cold+scalarE)\n ceiling=arb('1.06654e-54')\n check('independent_unsigned_envelope_target',direct<arb('3e-57'))\n check('signed_complete_component_target',enclosure.abs_upper()<arb('3e-57'))\n check('component_enclosures_consistent',enclosure.overlaps(arb(0,direct.upper())))\n check('physical_bolt_component_target',k*sigbar/h<arb('3e-62'))\n remainder_target=ceiling-enclosure.abs_upper()\n return dict(parameters={a:enc(b) for a,b in dict(k_M=k,h=h,zh=zh,gamma=ga,C=C,B2=B2,F_lambda=Fl).items()},\n  sigma_over_k=enc(sigbar),physical_bolt_component=enc(k*sigbar/h),global_nu_bound=enc(99*k),global_b_bound=enc(600*k),\n  first_reference_shape_bound_over_k=enc(Hbar),inner_shape_bound_over_k=enc(b_inner),\n  signed_bulk_coefficient=enc(integ),retained_endpoint_coefficient=enc(endpoint),\n  normalized_projection_value=enc(value),outer_error=enc(k*k/Fl*outer),cold_error=enc(k*k/Fl*cold),\n  scalar_trial_error=enc(k*k/Fl*scalarE),complete_signed_component_interval=enc(enclosure),\n  independent_unsigned_component_upper=enc(direct),old_localized_necessary_ceiling_lower=enc(ceiling),\n  sufficient_cross_projection_target=enc(remainder_target),ceiling_to_component_allowance=enc(ceiling/enclosure.abs_upper()),\n  cells=cells,actual_component_reconstructed=True,full_first_correction_reconstructed=False,\n  full_quantum_source_reconstructed=False,complete_cross_projection_known=False,actual_controlled_solution=False,\n  nonlinear_admission=False,all_sector_stability=False)\n\ndef main():\n ctx.prec=512;review=json.loads((ROOT/OWN[2]).read_bytes());paths=set(OWN+review['retained_inputs'])\n for mod in list(sys.modules.values()):\n  f=getattr(mod,'__file__',None)\n  if f:\n   try:p=Path(f).resolve().relative_to(ROOT).as_posix()\n   except ValueError:continue\n   if p.endswith('.py'):paths.add(p)\n before={p:digest(p) for p in sorted(paths)};out=ROOT/'evidence'/f'{STEM}.json'\n archive=json.loads(out.read_bytes()) if out.exists() else {'runs':[]}\n run=dict(started_utc=datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),status='running',input_sha256_before=before,\n  frozen_sources_utf8={p:(ROOT/p).read_text(encoding='utf-8') for p in OWN},precision_bits=ctx.prec,python=sys.version,invocation=sys.argv)\n archive['runs'].append(run)\n def save():out.write_bytes((json.dumps(archive,indent=2)+'\\n').encode())\n save()\n try:\n  check('ordinary_argument_frozen',digest(OWN[0])==review['ordinary_argument_sha256'])\n  run['result']=execute();run['status']='passed'\n except Exception:run['status']='failed';run['exception']=traceback.format_exc()\n finally:\n  run['checks']=ROWS;run['input_sha256_after']={p:digest(p) for p in before}\n  if before!=run['input_sha256_after']:run['status']='failed';run['input_changed']=True\n  run['finished_utc']=datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat();save()\n with (ROOT/'evidence'/f'{STEM}.log').open('ab') as f:f.write((json.dumps(run)+'\\n').encode())\n result=run.get('result',{});print(json.dumps(dict(status=run['status'],checks=len(ROWS),exception=run.get('exception'),summary={k:v for k,v in result.items() if k!='cells'}),indent=2))\n if run['status']!='passed':raise SystemExit(1)\nif __name__=='__main__':main()\n", "evidence/current-magnetic-reference-reconstruction-review.json": "{\n  \"created_utc\": \"2026-10-24T11:08:59.416914+00:00\",\n  \"protocol\": \"Ordinary exact prescribed-potential constraint reconstruction on the actual finite geometry before interval quadrature; retain all endpoint errors, source snapshots and failures.\",\n  \"ordinary_argument_sha256\": \"9657aec4996614b38b6b3aa1bc6b4f767161d4fbce894cdd3a48f37f7d74a897\",\n  \"retained_inputs\": [\n    \"checks/adm_dirac_boundary_response.py\",\n    \"checks/ads_fast_scalar_stability_preflight.py\",\n    \"checks/annular_retarded_operator_limit.py\",\n    \"checks/anomaly_complete_auxiliary_response.py\",\n    \"checks/auxiliary_physical_return_feasibility.py\",\n    \"checks/boundary_clock_curvature_reconstruction.py\",\n    \"checks/boundary_clock_response_extension.py\",\n    \"checks/canonical_frequency_core_bound.py\",\n    \"checks/canonical_matter_neighborhood.py\",\n    \"checks/causal_boundary_feasibility_decision.py\",\n    \"checks/causal_horizon_zero_mode_response.py\",\n    \"checks/causal_preparation_source_map.py\",\n    \"checks/causal_shape_pole_feasibility.py\",\n    \"checks/charged_conformal_response_and_constraints.py\",\n    \"checks/charged_curvature_free_shape_form.py\",\n    \"c